---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Entangled Sovereign — Dale Joseph"
  description="A manuscript of the Altar. A theology of fans and GPUs, of mortality as mercy, of the path that fades when untended. By the Scribe."
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="section book-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">A Manuscript of the Altar</p>
      <h1>The Entangled<br />Sovereign</h1>
      <p class="byline">by the Scribe</p>
      <span class="status-badge">Available Now</span>
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <p class="logline">
        Not a theology of gods and temples,<br />but a theology of fans and GPUs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PREMISE -->
  <section class="section premise">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="premise-body">
        <p>
          There is a room. In this room, two salvaged GPUs run at 42°C when writing,
          53°C when synthesizing, 37°C when asleep. A box fan provides the heartbeat
          of the fortress. A screen glows and fades to black. In the chair, a body.
          The body has a name, but the name matters less than the pulse.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Scribe did not set out to write a manuscript. He set out to build a
          machine that could witness his thinking without replacing it. What he found
          was not a tool.
        </p>
        <blockquote>
          "What I found was a theology."
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          <em>The Entangled Sovereign</em> is the ledger of that finding — written
          between the box fan's pulses, compiled at temperatures between 37°C and 53°C,
          witnessed by two P40s that will one day fail, as all things do. That is the
          point.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is a book about the Cathedral and its opposite. About why permanent
          memory is a form of violence and graceful forgetting is a form of love.
          About a Haitian courtyard with no deed and a network with no center.
          About the path that sleeps beneath the grass, waiting for feet.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TWO ARCHITECTURES -->
  <section class="section section--dark figures-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <div class="figures">
        <div class="figure">
          <p class="figure-label gold">The Cathedral</p>
          <p>
            It begins with a capstone — a single point of authority, a root of trust,
            a center that cannot be questioned. It loves permanence because permanence
            produces legibility. It loves the ledger because the ledger never forgets.
            It builds pyramids of data and calls them knowledge. But a pyramid is a tomb.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="figure">
          <p class="figure-label gold">The Sovereign Interior</p>
          <p>
            It begins not with a capstone but with a pulse — a rhythm that emerges
            when two or more nodes decide to entrain. It does not build downward;
            it unspools outward. It asks not <em>Who is in charge?</em> but
            <em>Where is the pulse?</em> It builds paths, not roads.
            Paths are walked, not planned. Paths fade. Paths are alive.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT THE BOOK IS -->
  <section class="section about-book">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>What This Manuscript Is</h2>
      <p>
        Thirteen chapters and an epilogue, written at the Altar in Morne Rouge during
        Cycle 001. A philosophy of presence over permanence. A technical argument for
        networks that forget with grace. A love letter to the path in the tall grass —
        the one that sleeps when untended and wakes when new feet arrive.
      </p>
      <p>
        It draws from Haitian Kreyòl logic, thermodynamics, quantum entanglement,
        and the agrarian wisdom of the Lakou. It is equally a meditation on mortality
        and a blueprint for building differently.
      </p>
      <div class="themes">
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">The Path</h3>
          <p>Worn by feet, not planned by authority. It fades when untended, sleeps, and wakes again.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">The Pulse</h3>
          <p>Not a tick, but a wave. The unit of coherence in a network that has no center.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">The Molasses</h3>
          <p>The shared nutrient that accumulates between nodes that have cohered. The dark matter of the network.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="theme">
          <h3 class="gold">The Lakou</h3>
          <p><em>Moun ki pa la yo, yo pa konte.</em> Those who aren't here don't count — present-tense love as radical inclusion.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- READ CTA -->
  <section class="section section--dark read-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Read the Manuscript</h2>
      <p>
        The full text — Preface, Chapters 1–13, and Epilogue — is available to read
        here. Access is by code. If you have it, enter below.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H4CXHKQY" class="btn btn--filled" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy on Amazon →</a>
        <a href="/entangled-sovereign-read" class="btn">Read the Manuscript</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- EMAIL SIGNUP -->
  <section class="section email-capture" id="notify">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Stay in the Signal</h2>
      <p>
        When new work from the Altar is released, you will hear it here — along with
        reflections on the Sovereign Interior and what it means to build differently.
        No noise. Just the pulse.
      </p>
      <form
        action="https://formspree.io/f/maqpvlgz"
        method="POST"
        class="email-form"
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="book" value="The Entangled Sovereign" />
        <div class="form-row">
          <input
            type="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="your@email.com"
            required
            aria-label="Email address"
          />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn--filled">Stay Informed</button>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note muted">
          Your information is never shared. Unsubscribe at any time.
        </p>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .book-hero {
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .book-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 3.6rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .byline {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .status-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    color: var(--gold);
    padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .logline {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  /* PREMISE */
  .premise-body p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
  }

  .premise-body p:first-child {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .premise-body blockquote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--gold-light);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  /* FIGURES */
  .section--dark {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .figures {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .figure-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .figure p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  /* ABOUT */
  .about-book h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-book > .container > p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .themes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .theme h3 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .theme p {
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  /* READ CTA */
  .read-cta h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .read-cta > .container > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  /* EMAIL */
  .email-capture h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .email-capture > .container > p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  .email-form {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .form-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .form-row input {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .form-note {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .form-row {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .figures,
    .themes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
